SCOPE OF WHAT IS COVERED

This file previously said only that third-party components keep their own
licenses. That is true but not specific enough to act on, because "the Software"
covers materials of four different kinds and they are not interchangeable. For
the avoidance of doubt, the terms above apply to the following, all owned by the
Owner:

  (a) SOURCE CODE — the Rust workspace under src-tauri/ (including the
      anima-domain crate), the TypeScript/React frontend under src/, the build
      and verification scripts under scripts/, and the test suites.

  (b) MODEL ARTIFACTS — trained or serialized network weights produced by this
      project, including any brain genotype or checkpoint files. Note that no
      pre-trained weights are distributed in this repository; weights are
      generated at runtime from a seed.

  (c) DATA FILES — generated world artifacts (.anmw), simulation save states,
      benchmark reports, and manifests, together with the formats that define
      them.

  (d) ASSETS — images, icons, and any visual or audio material under public/
      and src-tauri/icons/.

THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

The Software is distributed together with third-party components under
permissive licenses. Those components are NOT covered by this file and remain
governed by their own terms. They are inventoried in NOTICE, which is generated
from the dependency graph that is actually distributed
(`node scripts/gen_notice.mjs`) rather than hand-maintained.

NOTICE is an inventory, not a legal review. In particular it does not reproduce
the license texts that MIT and BSD require to accompany a distribution; the
packaging step does not yet copy them. That is a known open item.

